Expt. 9 (a) CPU task Stimulation in C.

Steps: 
(i) Open Ubuntu terminal.
(ii) Create a C program using: `nano expt 9.c`
(iii) Write the C program to stimulate a CPU intensive task using ∞ loop
(iv) Save and compile using: `gcc expt9.c -o expt9`
(v) Execute using `./expt9`
(vi) Observe the counter values displayed on the terminal.
(vii) Press Ctrl + C to terminate the program.
(viii) Enter the foll. command to monitor system processes and CPU utilization: `top`
(ix) Observe the CPU usage and running processes. Press q to exit and the top command.
